        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I bought all things Sentinels of the Multiverse at PAX AUstralia, having played the game once before and loving it.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I&#39;m reading through all the cards and have come across one that requires clarification (which I&#39;m sure has been asked before).</span></p><p>Kismet&#39;s Inconceivable Obstruction says:</p><blockquote><p>The first time each turn Kismet would be dealt damage, reveal the top card of the Environment deck. &nbsp;If it is a Target, put it into play and redirect the damage t it. &nbsp;If it is not a Target, discard it.</p></blockquote><p>So, does this mean that if the Environment deck card is not a Target, the damage still goes to Kismet?</p>",
